course: dictionary
lesson: 1821
title: Centimetres
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cm is short for centimetre, a small unit of length. We use it to say how long, wide or tall something is. There are 100 centimetres in one metre.
explain: Context helps you work out what a number means. «Holly, 140 cm, is taller than a metre.» The cm tells you the number is a length, and 140 cm is more than 100 cm, so it is more than a metre tall.
explain: In maths and science you will see cm² and cm³. Cm² means square centimetres, used for area. Cm³ means cubic centimetres, used for volume. Check the small number after cm before you answer.
fact: Cm is short for centimetre, which is also spelled centimeter.
fact: 100 cm make 1 metre.
fact: A centimetre is about the width of your little fingernail.
fact: The plural is still cm, so write «5 cm», not «5 cms». Cms is wrong.
fact: The giraffe's tongue is about 45 to 50 cm long, and it uses it to pull leaves from between thorns.
exercise: «Holly is 140 cm tall.» What does cm stand for? | Kilometre | Cabbage | *Centimetre | Count me
exercise: «The giraffe's tongue is about 45 to 50 cm long.» About how wide is one centimetre? | About the width of a door | About the length of your arm | A long bus | *About the width of your little fingernail
exercise: Which spelling is correct when you write about more than one? | cm's | cmes | cms | *cm
test: Holly is 140 cm tall and grows about 5 cm a year. About how tall will she be next year? | 5 cm | 135 cm | 160 cm | *145 cm
test: «A metre has how many centimetres?» | 10 | 50 | *100 | 1000
exam: «The area of the page is 40 square centimetres.» Which symbol means square centimetres? | cm/s | *cm² | cm³ | cm
